<Project>
  <!--
    Keeps this project's build output under the repo root's Build\ folder instead of a local
    bin\/obj\ next to the .csproj. $(MSBuildThisFileDirectory) always means "the folder this
    file is in" (Source\), regardless of which project imports it, so this stays correct even
    if invoked from elsewhere.

    BaseIntermediateOutputPath specifically must be set here rather than in the .csproj: NuGet's
    restore step reads it before Microsoft.Common.props is imported, so setting it inside the
    project file itself is too late and leaves a stray obj\ folder behind.

    The "DekUnrealGameAudit" segment is a literal, not a computed $(MSBuildProjectName) - WPF's
    build process generates a temporary shadow project (a "..._wpftmp.csproj") for markup
    compilation with its own generated name, which would compute a *different* path than the
    real project if this were name-derived. DekUnrealGameAudit.Gui.csproj has its own sibling
    Directory.Build.props in Gui\ for exactly this reason (MSBuild only auto-imports the
    closest one up the tree, so the two never conflict).
  -->
  <PropertyGroup>
    <BaseOutputPath>$(MSBuildThisFileDirectory)..\Build\bin\DekUnrealGameAudit\</BaseOutputPath>
    <BaseIntermediateOutputPath>$(MSBuildThisFileDirectory)..\Build\obj\DekUnrealGameAudit\</BaseIntermediateOutputPath>
  </PropertyGroup>
</Project>
